# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Veronica (VACA) — what is NOT tracked
#
# This repo holds the runnable app tree (Electron main process + payload).
# The two things that make a clone unrunnable on their own are deliberately
# excluded, because they are either huge or machine-specific:
#
#   1. the packaged release artifacts  -> attached to a GitHub Release
#   2. the Electron runtime + vendored node_modules -> installed / downloaded
#
# The LLM is excluded too, but it was never a file in here to begin with:
# see scripts/install-model.sh.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. packaged artifacts (GitHub Releases, not git) ─────────────────────────
# Two of these are over GitHub's 100 MB hard per-file limit, so git rejects
# them outright; keep them out of the index on purpose.
*.AppImage
*.deb
*.rpm
*.snap
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
*.zip
*.7z
# ANCHORED. A bare `dist/` matches at every level and would silently drop
# payload/backend/dist and payload/frontend/dist — i.e. the entire backend and
# the entire UI — leaving a repo that cannot run.
/dist/
/release/
SHA256SUMS

# ── 2a. the Electron runtime that wraps the app ──────────────────────────────
# Keep linux-unpacked/resources/app/** (our code) and ignore everything else in
# linux-unpacked/ (Chromium, the 218 MB `veronica` binary, locales, .pak, .so).
/linux-unpacked/*
!/linux-unpacked/resources/
/linux-unpacked/resources/*
!/linux-unpacked/resources/app/

# ── 2b. vendored dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# payload/node_modules is ~109 MB of install output. Restore it with:
#   npm --prefix linux-unpacked/resources/app/payload install
**/node_modules/

# ── 3. runtime state written by the backend ──────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── 4. machine-local config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dspark-target.env holds an absolute path to a GGUF on someone's workstation;
# dspark-target.env.example is the tracked, portable version.
*.env
!*.env.example
*.bak
*.bak-*
